    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by three core hitters who possess the highest projected efficiency scores: **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.34), **Jackson Merrill** (74.31), and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is an elite start at 1B, benefiting from a soft matchup against Martinez (4.80 xERA) and a favorable batting order position. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** is a priority play due to his high-percentage matchup against Elder, where the combination of the #2 spot and a positive park factor pushes his output toward the top tier. The most significant efficiency edge belongs to **Jacob Wilson**; facing Bratt (7.04 xERA), **Jacob Wilson** finds himself in an ideal \"green light\" situation, as the porous opposing pitching staff creates an elite environment for him to capitalize on his top-of-the-order responsibilities.\n\nWe are carefully monitoring **Andy Pages** (48.81) and **Sam Antonacci** (44.04), both of whom face high-skill arms (S\u00e1nchez and deGrom, respectively) that suppressed their ceiling scores. The closest call on the bench was **Curtis Mead** (53.51), who nearly displaced **Coby Mayo** (54.68) in the utility slot. While **Curtis Mead** carries strong park-factor adjustments, his projected platoon disadvantage against Freeland narrowed the gap, ultimately leading us to stick with **Coby Mayo** for his superior overall output projection. Caution is advised with **Gunnar Henderson** today; despite his talent, the matchup against Tolle\u2014combined with an unfavorable platoon split\u2014leaves him at a marginal 55.62, reinforcing the need to watch for early-game substitutions as we balance our game cap allocations across the roster.",
